# Database connection string.
# Copy this file to .env and set DATABASE_URL to your PostgreSQL connection string.
#
# For local dev we use Neon (serverless Postgres) — the same provider used in
# production, so dev and prod share the same kind of connection.
# 1. Create a project at https://neon.tech (free tier is enough).
# 2. In the dashboard, copy the connection string (Pooled, with password) for
#    the `neondb` database.
# 3. Replace the value below.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@EP-NAME.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"